  "helpTitle": "User guide",
  "helpHubSubtitle": "How to use every feature, and what to do if something goes wrong",
  "helpIntro": "MiFi replaces the modem's web interface. Tap a topic to learn how to use each feature.",
  "helpStartTitle": "Getting started",
  "helpStartBody": "1. Connect the phone to the modem's Wi-Fi (name and password are on the modem's label).\n2. Open MiFi and enter the modem's admin password (printed on the label if it was never changed).\n3. Keep “Remember password” checked: you will be signed in automatically next time. The password is stored encrypted on the phone.\n\nIf Android says this Wi-Fi has “No internet access” (for example when data is off), that is normal: the app still uses it to talk to the modem.",
  "helpAddressTitle": "Modem address",
  "helpAddressBody": "By default, the modem answers at 192.168.100.1.\n\nIf you change it under “Local network (DHCP)”, the app automatically follows the new address. You can also change it by hand on the sign-in screen (“Modem address”) or in Settings › App settings. The app suggests the current Wi-Fi gateway address when it differs.",
  "helpDashboardTitle": "Dashboard",
  "helpDashboardBody": "At the top, as in the original interface: Wi-Fi, SIM, signal and internet icons, the operator name, the language picker and the admin menu (password, guide, sign out).\n\nBelow: the signal (bars, dBm, quality), the internet state and WAN IP, phone-style quick toggles (Mobile data, Wi-Fi, USB sharing), “Restart the connection”, connected devices, modem information and versions, and shortcuts.\n\nData refreshes continuously (every 2 seconds); pull down to reload everything. Values the modem does not provide are hidden instead of showing 0.",
  "helpOperatorTitle": "Operator and SIM change",
  "helpOperatorBody": "The app works with any operator's SIM. It shows the service name provided by the SIM; otherwise it derives the operator from the SIM code (MTN, Orange, Nexttel, Camtel), or shows “Operator 624-XX”.\n\nWhen you change SIM, the app shows “New SIM detected” and offers to open the APN settings. The modem usually picks the right APN by itself.",
  "helpMobileDataTitle": "Mobile data",
  "helpMobileDataBody": "As on a phone, the “Mobile data” toggle cuts the internet while keeping the SIM on the network (the signal stays visible). Wi-Fi stays on.\n\nSince the modem has no dedicated command, the app activates a blocking APN profile (“MiFi-OFF”); turning data back on restores your usual profile. A “Mobile data” tile is also available in Android Quick Settings.",
  "helpAirplaneTitle": "Airplane mode",
  "helpAirplaneBody": "As on a phone, airplane mode cuts the internet on the SIM in use (SIM 1 or SIM 2), without ever changing SIM. After confirmation, it turns on in a few seconds. The modem's Wi-Fi stays on: your devices stay connected to the modem (without internet) and the app can always turn airplane mode off.\n\nThe modem has no command to turn its radio off: the app cuts the internet by activating a blocking APN profile (“MiFi-OFF”). The SIM therefore stays on the network and the signal bars stay visible. If you change SIM during airplane mode, the cut also applies to the new SIM.\n\nThe app checks that the connection drops. If the modem switches back to its usual APN profile by itself, the app re-applies the cut: at every refresh while the app is open, otherwise during background checks (every 15 minutes at best, if they are enabled). If the cut doesn't hold, for example when the carrier accepts any APN, a warning is shown.\n\nDuring airplane mode, the “Mobile data” toggle is greyed out. Turning airplane mode off restores your usual APN profile.",
  "helpReconnectTitle": "Restart the connection and automatic repair",
  "helpReconnectBody": "When the internet stops working, tap “Restart the connection” on the dashboard: the app cuts the modem's connection, like airplane mode (it registers on the network again), then restores it. It tries again until the internet is back or until you tap “Stop”; the attempt number and elapsed time are shown. It is much faster than restarting the modem, which is still offered.\n\nWith automatic repair (Settings › App settings), the app does it by itself if the internet has been down for 3 minutes with a good signal (3 attempts at most, at most once every 30 minutes).",
  "helpTileTitle": "Quick Settings tiles and shortcuts",
  "helpTileBody": "To turn mobile data on or off without opening the app:\n1. Swipe down twice from the top of the screen.\n2. Tap the pencil (Edit).\n3. Drag MiFi's “Mobile data” tile among your tiles.\n\nA tap starts the change. The phone must be connected to the modem's Wi-Fi and the password remembered; if it fails, a notification tells you.\n\nA long press on the MiFi icon also offers shortcuts: Share Wi-Fi, Speed test.",
  "helpWidgetTitle": "Home screen widgets",
  "helpWidgetBody": "Long-press an empty spot of the home screen, choose “Widgets”, then MiFi: the “Modem status” widget shows the operator, signal, internet and number of devices; a tap opens the app. It updates while the app is open and at each background check.",
  "helpScheduleTitle": "Scheduled restart",
  "helpScheduleBody": "In Settings › App settings › Automation, the scheduled restart restarts the modem every day at the chosen time.\n\nAt the scheduled time, the phone must be connected to the modem's Wi-Fi; otherwise a failure notification is shown. Android may shift the time by a few minutes.",
  "helpDevicesTitle": "Connected devices",
  "helpDevicesBody": "The Devices tab lists connected devices: name, type (Wi-Fi or wired), IP address and MAC address. Tap a device to give it a nickname, remembered by its MAC address.\n\nA “New” badge marks a device seen for the first time recently, and an alert warns you when an unknown device connects, with direct access to “Kick out intruders”. Devices seen before but disconnected are listed separately.",
  "helpExpelTitle": "Kick out intruders",
  "helpExpelBody": "The modem cannot block a device. “Kick out intruders” generates a strong new Wi-Fi password (12 characters), applies it and immediately shows its QR code. You can also hide the Wi-Fi name to make it invisible to neighbours.\n\nAll devices, including this phone, are disconnected: reconnect them with the new password (“Reconnect this phone” button, QR code or share by message). The app resumes its session as soon as the phone is reconnected.",
  "helpWifiTitle": "Wi-Fi and sharing",
  "helpWifiBody": "Settings › Wi-Fi lets you change the network name, the password (8 to 32 characters), the security, the channel and whether the name is broadcast. After saving, the Wi-Fi restarts: reconnect the phone to the network.\n\nTo share the Wi-Fi: a QR code to scan with the camera, or send the name and password by message (WhatsApp, SMS…).\n\nWarning: “Turn off Wi-Fi” disconnects the phone immediately and the app will not be able to turn it back on. You will need the modem's button or a restart.",
  "helpDhcpTitle": "Local network (DHCP)",
  "helpDhcpBody": "This page sets the modem address, the netmask, the range of addresses given to devices and the lease time (in hours). The app checks that the range is in the same subnet as the modem.\n\nSaving restarts the modem (about 1 minute). If the modem address changes, the app automatically uses the new one. The DHCP server state is shown read-only.",
  "helpMobileTitle": "Mobile network",
  "helpMobileBody": "• SIM card: slot in use (SIM 1 or SIM 2); switching takes about 20 seconds.\n• Mobile data: same toggle as on the dashboard.\n• APN: choose the profile used for the internet or create one with your operator's settings (MCC and MNC are pre-filled from the SIM).\n• Network mode: automatic 4G/3G, 4G only or 3G only.\n• USB tethering: internet over a USB cable to a computer.\n• Outage detection: the modem checks the connection by contacting these addresses (IP or name, for example 8.8.8.8 or www.google.com).",
  "helpSystemTitle": "System",
  "helpSystemBody": "• Change the admin password: the app signs in again by itself with the new one.\n• Restart the modem: about 1 minute; the app waits for it to come back.\n• Factory reset: two confirmations are required. Wi-Fi and password go back to the values on the modem's label: reconnect the phone to the factory Wi-Fi, then sign in again. Make a backup first.\n• Manufacturing information: factory calibration and Wi-Fi test (read-only).",
  "helpFirmwareTitle": "Firmware update",
  "helpFirmwareBody": "For advanced users only: a wrong file can make the modem unusable.\n\nBefore starting: battery charged, modem plugged in and not moving, phone close to the modem. Choose the official .zip file (500 MB maximum) and enter the CRC code provided with it. During the upload, do not leave the app and do not turn the modem off. At the end, the modem updates and restarts.",
  "helpSignalTitle": "Signal history and best location",
  "helpSignalBody": "Settings › Signal history shows the signal strength (in dBm) over the last hour or the last 24 hours. The closer to 0, the better: excellent (4 bars) from -80 dBm, good (3) from -90, fair (2) from -100, poor (1) from -110, none below; bars are green, orange or red depending on the level. The reading is updated continuously (every 2 seconds).\n\n“Find the best location” shows a large gauge updated every 2 to 3 seconds. Move the modem slowly (near a window, up high) and wait a few seconds at each spot: the app remembers the best value.",
  "helpOutagesTitle": "Outage log",
  "helpOutagesBody": "Each internet loss is recorded with its start, end and duration; outages caused by data turned off or by “Restart the connection” are marked “planned”. A summary shows the number and duration of outages over 24 hours and 7 days.\n\nThe export button saves the log as a CSV file (readable with Excel), for example to complain to the operator.",
  "helpSpeedTestTitle": "Speed test and operator comparison",
  "helpSpeedTestBody": "The speed test downloads a file (5, 10 or 25 MB) through the modem and shows the speed in Mb/s with its quality: none, poor, fair, good or excellent. It uses data from your plan. Results are kept in a history.\n\nThe operator comparison (shortcut on the dashboard) groups, for each SIM used over the last 7 days: average signal, average speed and outages. Handy to choose the SIM that works best where you are.",
  "helpBackupTitle": "Backup and restore",
  "helpBackupBody": "“Export the settings” saves the Wi-Fi, APN, DHCP, network mode and outage detection settings to a file. The admin password is never exported, but the file contains the Wi-Fi password: keep it safe.\n\n“Restore” re-applies a backup, for example after a factory reset. You choose the sections; DHCP restarts the modem, and Wi-Fi is applied last because the phone will have to reconnect to it.",
  "helpNotificationsTitle": "Notifications",
  "helpNotificationsBody": "MiFi can warn you when the internet goes down or comes back, when the signal is weak and when a new device connects. Set them up in Settings › App settings › Notifications, and allow them when Android asks.\n\nWhile the app is open, monitoring is continuous. When it is closed, continuous monitoring (App settings) alerts you within seconds; without it, Android only allows a check about every 15 minutes. The phone must be connected to the modem's Wi-Fi.",
  "helpLanguageTitle": "Language, theme and lock",
  "helpLanguageBody": "In Settings › App settings:\n• app language (phone language, French or English); the “Also apply to the modem's web interface” option also changes the language of the original web page;\n• automatic, light or dark theme;\n• lock: MiFi asks for the fingerprint or the phone's code when it opens.",
  "helpTroubleshootingTitle": "Troubleshooting",
  "helpTroubleshootingBody": "• “Cannot reach the modem”: check that the phone is connected to the modem's Wi-Fi, then the modem address (192.168.100.1 by default).\n• “Session expired”: the app signs in again by itself; if the password was changed elsewhere, sign in again.\n• Wi-Fi turned off: turn it back on with the modem's button or restart the modem.\n• Forgotten admin password: do a factory reset with the modem's RESET button.\n• Mobile data failed: check the Wi-Fi and try again; as a last resort, restart the modem.",
  "helpLimitsTitle": "What the modem cannot do",
  "helpLimitsBody": "The modem's API does not provide this information, and the app does not make it up: battery level, data used, blocking a device, SMS, USSD, operator balance or plan.",
